150-assembly to temperatures generally between 100°C to 
151:150°C. The most critical parameter in the preheat section 
152-is to minimize the rate of rise to less than 2”C/second. 
153-The main concern is minimizing thermal shock on the 
154-components of the assembly. Multilayer ceramic chip 
155-capacitors can be vulnerable to cracking if heated too 
156-fast. Solder paste can spatter also, if heated too fast. 
