312-AT = Product Temperature Rise (“C) 
313-Q = Heat Absorbed (w/cmz) 
314-A = Exposed Area (cm2) 
315:t = Heating Dwell Time (seconds) 
316-M = Mass of Object (kg) 
317-Cp = Specific Heat (w-sec/kg-”C) 
318-The mass (M) times the specific heat (Cp) is often referred 
319-to as thermal mass. Greater thermal mass requires more 
320-heat to achieve a given temperature rise. In the figure 
