336-OVEN UNIFORMITY 
337-A second main cause of non-uniform product heating is 
338-the oven heating pattern. This can be caused by edge 
339-effects on the heaters (less heat at the end) or by heat 
340:sinking of the conveyor system. The edge effect may be 
341-caused by insufficient airflow around the edges of the 
342-machine, or by non-uniformities that are inherent in the 
343:heaters. The heat sinking of the conveyor is really amass 
344-effect, similar to the one described above. The oven 
345-uniformity may be measured by thermocoupling a bare 
346-board over a matrix of points, and running a profile. The 
347-matrix should include points on the board edges (front, 
348-back, left, and right), and the center of the board. 
